  "name": "Back in the fixer queue after capacity_exhausted",
  "notes": "#39: a fixer try whose agent hit its backend's usage limit (capacity_exhausted). The built-in fixer.cooldown first rests that try's level: it upserts fixer_cooldowns/<the level's actor> until the try's end plus vars.fixer_capacity_cooldown_s (default 3600 s), the actor read from the failed run's own agent step (never from an input), and only for an actor of vars.fixer_levels. Then the built-in queue.add puts the story back in line as a retry, so queue.progress gives its next try the next available level. The failed try still counts toward the story's 3; one whose PR spent them fails here and the rule hands back once. Non-agentic: no actor, no GitHub call.",
